  "body": "Found during the work on issue 1735.\n\n## Problem\n\nIssue 1735 made two open edges a band that the stock outline closes. When the two edges, run on straight, meet inside the stock, the band has one open end only. The operation refuses that selection by name: \"the two picked open edges run together inside the stock - the band between them has one open end only ...\". Edges at more than 45 degrees to each other are also refused.\n\n## Wanted\n\n- Decide if a wedge between two edges that meet inside the stock is a valid region.\n- If it is valid, define the region exactly and write the definition in a decision record.\n- Decide if the 45 degree limit stays.\n\n## Safety\n\nThe gouge check and the collision check must not change. A selection that is not clear must stay refused by name.\n\n## Done means\n\nA decision record gives the definition or keeps the refusal, and tests pin the result.\n\nPart of the work that started with #1735.\n",
